{:activity/_scope [{:activity/expected-seconds 600.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116102} :activity/id #uuid "18afd5ba-844e-5a0a-b7f3-a142f4f4628b" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050446} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116102 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116488 :tutorial/content "Powers of matrices are similar to powers of numbers. If $A$ is a matrix, then $A^n$ is $A$ multiplied by itself $n$ times: \n\n$$\nA^n = \\underbrace{A\\:\\cdot\\: A\\:\\cdot\\: \\ldots \\:\\cdot\\: A}_{\\Large{n\\text{ times}}}\n$$\n\nFor $A$ to be conformable with itself, $A$ needs to be a square matrix. So we can only take powers of square matrices.\n\nTo demonstrate, suppose that\n![](images/81/81537bed0eafc982114b89fc84baeac44f7a75997c89df5a0f89b8b0a00b2da3.svg)\n\nThen we can calculate $A^2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot 2 & 3\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 1 \\\\ 2\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 2 & 2\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -4 \\\\ 8 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe say that $A^0 = I,$ the identity matrix of the same dimension as $A.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "ee44491b-6b6b-5f87-9b67-ffc9a32397f7" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2999 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "fb346f38-313a-573c-b90a-fbbe590dbd2f" :step/math-academy-id 16200 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116103}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116103 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115229 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115059 :question/id #uuid "f832e671-b4bd-5d1d-81e7-b215a8ee4e27" :question/math-academy-id "e-4414" :question/problem "Find $A^4$ given that ![](images/e0/e0e7d5ed9b893352d68931ff5d8fa93f0d0c5173e5955a3f5cdc0cb65d3c3c78.svg)" :question/worked-solution "First, to find $A^2,$ we multiply $A$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $A^4 = A^2 \\cdot A^2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{4} & ={A}^{2}\\cdot {A}^{2} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}9 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}81 & 0 \\\\ 100 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e970fe-cff8-50e3-9b94-67ad97b03da7" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050407} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050668}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534214 :question-generator/id #uuid "531c64e5-3195-5fc7-908c-a759be9ac756" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186115229.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115763 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a9c8943-d512-59d8-ae9d-b3da2c5a7ee9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 4 \\\\ 16 & 49\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113545} {:answer/id #uuid "b2fd1097-ab0f-59d6-b5bc-67d1a5b18177" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113546} {:answer/id #uuid "3286c77e-84a0-5e1e-bb91-dde5502f759b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 20 \\\\ -40 & 41\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113547} {:answer/id #uuid "4f49f2d3-8b68-5f8d-8307-5aef368b4728" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113548} {:answer/id #uuid "6abdcd80-6f13-54f4-b576-632d85a3528a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}17 & 20 \\\\ -16 & 57\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113549}] :answer-field/id #uuid "22fbf2de-