er-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25168437-2aa4-5977-952c-2051730ceff6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485826} {:answer/id #uuid "5b213e2b-cc6d-508a-a15f-3bf22cc91d0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485924} {:answer/id #uuid "8b991cf9-c833-51b6-a70c-6462ead85a65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486013} {:answer/id #uuid "caf9fadd-4204-560a-bbdd-f5a3d57450f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 1 \\\\ 20 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486132} {:answer/id #uuid "e0dd670b-075f-5794-a254-3720ba484dbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}11 & 1 \\\\ 20 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486176}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485924} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab274d63-ed23-5349-8036-9b61afae1797" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486307}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ebea1a9b-d1dc-56a2-8933-0092e4727688" :question/math-academy-id "q-130673" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.$  Find $f(A)$ if $f(X)={X}^{2}+X-1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}+X-1 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}+X-I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(A)={A}^{2}+A-I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${A}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(A):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & ={A}^{2}+A-I \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1+3-1 & 0-2+0 \\\\ 0+4+0 & 1-3-1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Matrix Polynomial"} :step/id #uuid "f98ae8b7-d09c-5763-8545-e0528e7956df" :step/math-academy-id 16205}] :activity/title "Powers of Matrices" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186115471}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186050446 :topic/difficulty 0.8032068134483066 :topic/encompasses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186428317 :encompassing/rationale "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 1 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction = 1. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1 (1/1). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: False. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/foundations-frequency-estimates.json, pair 1725->1198. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json." :encompassing/topic {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783} :encompassing/weight 1.0}] :topic/id #uuid "49ac363b-d07a-55f5-9f5d-8e58eafc76b5" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/